---

srapnol is the SQP Reduced-Hessian Active-Set Partitioning Nonlinear Optimization Library. Its method is sequential quadratic programming in the style of Gill, Murray and Saunders.

A problem is given as `F(x) = f(x) + A x`, with bounds on `x` and `F`, a constant sparse `A`, and a sparse Jacobian supplied by the user for the nonlinear part `f`.

It is an early project, developed with a controlled set of documentation to NASA's software engineering standards.
